(SOP-WH-005: DISPATCH AND LOADING PROCEDURE) Tj T*
(Version: 2.2) Tj T*
(Effective Date: 2026-09-20) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. PURPOSE) Tj T*
(This procedure defines the checks and actions required before goods leave the warehouse on) Tj T*
(  outbound vehicles.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. BEFORE LOADING) Tj T*
(2.1 Verify the vehicle temperature is at range before loading chilled or frozen orders.) Tj T*
(  Chilled: 2 to 8 degrees Celsius. Frozen: minus 18 degrees Celsius or below.) Tj T*
(2.2 Confirm the route manifest matches the vehicle number. Loading against the wrong manifest) Tj T*
(  is a critical error and must be reported the same day.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. LOADING SEQUENCE) Tj T*
(3.1 Load in reverse drop order: the last delivery is loaded first.) Tj T*
(3.2 Heavy cartons on the floor, light cartons on top. Do not stack above the load line marked) Tj T*
(  inside the vehicle.) Tj T*
(3.3 Seal the vehicle after loading and record the seal number on the manifest.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. PRE-DEPARTURE CHECKS) Tj T*
(4.1 The dispatcher must confirm all cartons on the manifest are loaded. Any missing carton) Tj T*
(  blocks departure until located.) Tj T*
(4.2 Hand the driver the signed manifest and the temperature log printout for chilled loads.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. WHAT MUST BE CHECKED BEFORE DISPATCHING GOODS - SUMMARY) Tj T*
(Before dispatching goods, the operator must verify: vehicle temperature at range, route) Tj T*
(  manifest matches the vehicle, all cartons loaded, seal applied and recorded, and driver) Tj T*
(  documentation handed over. Dispatch is not permitted with any open food-safety hold or) Tj T*
(  quality hold flag on the order.) Tj T*
ET
